{
  "cell": "ro_ring5_wstv0p48",
  "_comment": [
    "ro_ring5_wstv0p48 -- design/ro_array_core.spice's `.subckt ro_ring5` at wstv=0.48 um,",
    "i.e. the physical cell for one of ro_array_core's four non-identical rings",
    "(xr1-xr4 instantiate ro_ring5 at wstv 0.42/0.44/0.46/0.48; see",
    "layout/README.md's 'Starve-width variants' section and DR-0003 Section 8",
    "for why the rings are deliberately not the same cell).",
    "",
    "Byte-for-byte identical to layout/ro_ring5/cell.json except for the two",
    "leaf gds_path/cell_name pairs and lvs.params.wstv. That is not an",
    "assumption: all four wstv variants of ro_stage and of ro_nand2 have",
    "identical cell bboxes, identical merged-nwell bboxes and identical",
    "merged-met1 bboxes (verified directly from the committed GDS), because",
    "the width variation is absorbed inside each leaf by re-deriving Mph/Mnt's",
    "own placement origin rather than by growing the cell. Every origin, lane",
    "and waypoint in layout/ro_ring5/cell.json therefore transfers unchanged.",
    "See layout/ro_ring5/README.md for the derivation of each number."
  ],
